{"type":"message","id":"d0d3d4f8","parentId":"ed9903e0","timestamp":"2026-03-26T14:11:28.341Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to update the portfolio. The A50 position needs to be updated with the new price. The entry was 100, and now A50 closed at 14,529 points (down 1%).\n\nWait, I need to understand the pricing. In the portfolio.json:\n- A50 entry_price: 100\n- A50 current_price: 98.3 (from yesterday)\n- A50 index_close: 14474.97 (yesterday's close)\n\nSo the \"100\" and \"98.3\" are not the actual index values, but some normalized values. Let me calculate based on the percentage change.\n\nFrom yesterday to today:\n- Yesterday A50: 14474.97 points\n- Today A50: 14529.0 points (down 1% from yesterday's close)\n\nWait, that doesn't make sense. Let me re-read the search results:\n\n\"富时中国A50指数期货跌幅扩大至1%，最新报14529.0点\"\n\nBut yesterday's close was 14474.97. If today is 14529.0, that's actually an increase, not a decrease. Let me check the percentage:\n\n(14529.0 - 14474.97) / 14474.97 = 54.03 / 14474.97 = 0.00373 = 0.373% increase\n\nSo today A50 is up 0.37%, not down 1%. The \"跌幅扩大至1%\" might be referring to intraday movement from the opening.\n\nSo the current normalized price should be:\n- Yesterday: 98.3\n- Today: 98.3 * (14529.0 / 14474.97) = 98.3 * 1.00373 = 98.67\n\nLet me update the portfolio with this new price.\n\nCurrent position:\n- Entry: 100\n- Yesterday close: 98.3 (unrealized loss: -1.7%)\n\n\n- Today close: 98.67 (unrealized loss: -1.33%)\n\nI've calculated the new position value and loss percentage. The position has improved slightly, with the loss decreasing from -1.7% to -1.33%. This represents a small positive movement in the A50 index.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"019d2a7c42b52407c5696694b914ac26","name":"edit","arguments":{"file_path":"/workspace/projects/workspace/paper-trading/portfolio.json","oldText":"      \"symbol\": \"A50\",\n      \"name\": \"FTSE C